      "body": "## Overview\r\n\r\nCut the ROCM_AITER_FA sliding-window decode-table trim (`_build_swa_decode_tables`, q == 1 decodes) from 10 aten ops to 7 per call, with byte-identical results.\r\n\r\nThis PR started as an opt-in trim of the block table for spec-decode verify (q > 1), which only paid off with a window-bounded AITER split. AITER instead merged a window-aware split, ROCm/aiter#6889 (`b6c376cfa6`). Its split covers only each sequence's window tiles, so an untrimmed verify table gets the same split as a trimmed one, and the verify trim would only add ops. That part and `VLLM_ROCM_AITER_FA_SWA_VERIFY_TRIM` are dropped. vLLM picks up the AITER split with the next AITER bump; main pins v0.1.27, which predates it.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- 7 aten ops per call instead of 10. The old ops were `sub`, `clamp`, `floor_divide`, `_to_copy`, `add`, `clamp_`, `gather`, `mul`, `sub`, `copy_`; the new ones are `sub`, `clamp_`, `floor_divide`, `add`, `clamp_`, `gather`, `sub`.\r\n- The table, seq lens and max seq len are byte-identical to the previous formula.\r\n- The table is built once per decode step for each sliding-window KV-cache group.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nIn a ROCm image with no GPU work (the branch's source over the image's compiled vLLM):\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ pytest tests/v1/attention/test_rocm_aiter_fa_swa_decode_tables.py\r\n1 passed\r\n```\r\n\r\n- The new CPU test compares the trimmed table, seq lens (and their dtype) and max seq len with the previous formula. It covers contexts across the window and block edges, from 1 to 200000.\r\n- A mutant that rebases the seq lens by one block too many fails it.\r\n- Op counts come from a `TorchDispatchMode` counter over the old and new code on the same inputs, which also confirms identical outputs.\r\n- `tests/kernels/attention/test_rocm_aiter_fa.py` (GPU, unchanged) still runs the q == 1 trimmed table through AITER `paged_attention_v1` against the full table.\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\n- The clamp of the first visible key runs in place.\r\n- `_swa_block_offsets` is int64, so adding it promotes the gather index and the int64 cast copy is not needed.\r\n- The rebased seq lens are written straight into the persistent buffer with `torch.sub(lens, first_block, alpha=block_size, out=...)`, instead of a temporary followed by `copy_`.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n\r\n</details>",
